<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan Willem Janssens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1762">1762</a>–<a href="/years/1838">1838</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan Willem Janssens was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> general and colonial governor. As governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a> from 1803 he was defeated by the British in 1806, and as governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> he surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> to a British invasion force in September 1811. He later served as Dutch minister of war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-willem-janssens.jpg" alt="Jan Willem Janssens" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Willem Pieneman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jonkheer_Jan_Willem_Janssens_(1762-1838)._Gouverneur_van_de_Kaapkolonie_en_gouverneur-generaal_van_Nederlands_Oost_Indi%C3%AB_Rijksmuseum_SK-A-2219.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
